# THE CONTRACT CANARY — DO NOT REMOVE THIS ENTRY.
#
# In this file LINE POSITION IS SEMANTIC: `@ts-expect-error` suppresses errors on
# the NEXT LINE ONLY. Prettier reflowing a single-line object literal into a
# multi-line one pushes the offending property down, so the directive stops
# covering it. That fails in the nastiest possible way — the directive reports as
# unused (TS2578) AND the error it was hiding escapes (TS2322), on a file whose
# entire job is to be the early-warning system for a broken contract freeze.
#
# This is not hypothetical; it happened when prettier was first introduced.
# Format this file by hand or not at all.
